{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/agent-source && sed -n \"$(grep -n '\"'func (n \\\\*node) processReadyToRead' node.go | cut -d: -f1),+20p\\\" node.go\"","aggregated_output":"func (n *node) processReadyToRead(ud pb.Update) {\n\tif len(ud.ReadyToReads) > 0 {\n\t\tn.pendingReadIndexes.addReady(ud.ReadyToReads)\n\t\tn.pendingReadIndexes.applied(ud.LastApplied)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) processSnapshot(ud pb.Update) error {\n\tif !pb.IsEmptySnapshot(ud.Snapshot) {\n\t\terr := n.logReader.ApplySnapshot(ud.Snapshot)\n\t\tif err != nil && !isSoftSnapshotError(err) {\n\t\t\treturn errors.Wrapf(err, \"%s failed to apply snapshot\", n.id())\n\t\t}\n\t\tplog.Debugf(\"%s, push snapshot %d\", n.id(), ud.Snapshot.Index)\n\t\tn.pushSnapshot(ud.Snapshot, ud.LastApplied)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) applyRaftUpdates(ud pb.Update) {\n\tn.pushEntries(n.entriesToApply(ud.CommittedEntries))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id']=='af06927cb2104482944345b4c982f0d9-interpretation-0'][0]\nprint(v['rationale'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id']=='af06927cb2104482944345b4c982f0d9-interpretation-0'][0]\nprint(v['rationale'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"The suspicion that a granted vote could be lost before the vote response is sent is refuted for the captured batch path. processSteps takes one update per active node, emits only the messages that isFreeOrderMessage classifies as free order, which is Replicate and Ping, and then calls SaveRaftState for the whole batch; the log DB contract says that call atomically saves the raft states, log entries and snapshot metadata, and the implementation puts each non-empty state and the entries into one write batch that it commits once. The remaining messages travel in the same update through processRaftUpdate, which runs only after that commit, so RequestVoteResp, HeartbeatResp, ReplicateResp and ReadIndexResp are all emitted after the state that justifies them is durable. A crash after a vote response therefore cannot leave the previous vote or term in place, and the node cannot grant a different vote in the same term. The pre-persistence Replicate and Ping emission is the deliberate exception documented at the call site with a reference to section 10.2.1 of the Raft thesis; those messages carry no granted authority of their own, so the ordering that matters for election safety is preserved. The refutation covers the ordering of the local atomic write batch, not the durability guarantees of a specific storage engine.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nout={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Prevent a misreading of the pre-save readiness release. processReadyToRead does not complete a read when it runs: it passes the signals to pendingReadIndex.addReady and then applies LastApplied, and pendingReadIndex.applied completes a batch only when the applied index reaches its ready index. The entry is corrected to state that completion condition, so the early release is described as recording a ready index rather than completing a read. The vote-durability conclusion is unaffected because that release carries no election state.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n  \\\"id\\\":\\\"663619265b3c4d409e03385d0f091c3e-knowledge-0\\\",\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"engine.processSteps takes one update per active node, calls applySnapshotAndUpdate, then for each update sends the free-order messages (Replicate and Ping) and calls processReadyToRead, processDroppedEntries and processDroppedReadIndexes, and only after that calls logdb.SaveRaftState for the whole batch. The remaining messages, including vote responses and read-index replies, are released by node.processRaftUpdate after the save. processReadyToRead passes its signals to pendingReadIndex.addReady and then applies LastApplied, and a batch completes only when the applied index reaches its ready index, so the pre-save release records a ready index without completing a read.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"The updates come from the engine's batch loop, each node includes its changed raft state, and the log DB implements SaveRaftState as one atomically committed write batch.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"engine-process-steps\\\",\\\"node-free-order-messages\\\",\\\"node-process-ready\\\"],\n  \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"The earlier statement recorded only that readiness signals reach the node layer before the batch is persisted. It now also records that processReadyToRead completes a batch only when LastApplied reaches the ready index, so the early release does not complete a read before the entries are applied.\\\",\n  \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"af06927cb2104482944345b4c982f0d9-interpretation-0\\\"]\n }]\n}\njson.dump(out, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance && .venv/bin/consensus-assurance validate --run runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
